2006,"icon":"🥇","title":"China Overtakes the US","text":"China becomes the world's #1 CO2 emitter for the first time in history."},{"t":2008.9,"icon":"📉","title":"Financial Crisis Hits","text":"Global emissions dip in 2009 for the first time since the early 1990s."},{"t":2013.5,"icon":"🇮🇳","title":"India Passes Russia","text":"India's rapid growth pushes it past Russia into the 4th largest emitter spot."},{"t":2015.92,"icon":"🌍","title":"Paris Agreement Adopted","text":"196 countries pledge to hold warming well below 2°C above pre-industrial levels."},{"t":2020.3,"icon":"🦠","title":"COVID-19 Emissions Crash","text":"Global lockdowns cut world CO2 emissions by roughly 5% in a single year."},{"t":2021.6,"icon":"🔺","title":"Record Post-Covid Rebound","text":"Emissions jump over 6% in 2021, the largest single-year rise on record."},{"t":2023.5,"icon":"📈","title":"All-Time Emissions Record","text":"World fossil CO2 emissions hit an all-time high of about 37.8 billion tonnes."},{"t":2024,"icon":"🌱","title":"China's Emissions Plateau?","text":"Analysts report China's CO2 output may be peaking as solar and EV growth surges."}],"sources":[{"title":"Our World in Data – CO2 and Greenhouse Gas Emissions (Global Carbon Project)","url":"https://ourworldindata.org/co2-emissions"},{"title":"OWID co2-data GitHub repository","url":"https://github.com/owid/co2-data"},{"title":"Our World in Data – Annual CO2 emissions by country (grapher)","url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/annual-co2-emissions-per-country"},{"title":"List of countries by carbon dioxide emissions – Wikipedia (OWID/Global Carbon Project sourced table)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_carbon_dioxide_emissions"},{"title":"Global Carbon Budget 2023 / 2024","url":"https://globalcarbonbudget.org/fossil-co2-emissions-at-record-high-in-2023/"}],"notes":"Metric: territorial CO2 emissions from fossil fuels and industry (cement etc.), excluding land-use change, in tonnes CO2/year. Exact anchor values for 2000 and 2023 for most countries were taken from Our World in Data / Global Carbon Project figures (via Wikipedia's summary table). All other years, including all of 1960-1999 and 2001-2022 except stated anchors, plus 2024, are interpolated or estimated by the research desk from known historical trajectories (industrialization curves, oil shocks, USSR collapse, financial crisis, COVID dip) because a full year-by-year machine-readable extract could not be retrieved in this session — treat these as reasonable approximations, not official published values. Germany pre-1990 values are combined West+East Germany estimates; Russia pre-1991 values are Russian SFSR territorial estimates consistent with OWID's long-run series. 2024 figures are preliminary/estimated pending final Global Carbon Budget confirmation. World total is the actual global fossil+industry CO2 total (not simply the sum of the 16 shown countries, which represent roughly 70% of global emissions). Data licensed CC BY 4.0 by Our World in Data / Global Carbon Project.","music":{"prompt":"Epic cinematic instrumental that mirrors a century of rising industrial output: begins with a lone sparse piano and soft low strings in D minor, slowly layering deep brass swells, driving low cello ostinato and tense timpani hits as the piece builds, tempo 88 BPM, dramatic rising string runs and choir-like pads entering at the climax to evoke record-breaking global emissions, ending on a suspended, unresolved chord to suggest an uncertain future. Instrumental only, no vocals.","style":"cinematic","bpm":88,"key":"D","scale":"minor","progression":[1,6,4,5],"motif":[1,3,5,8,5,3,1,0,6,8,10,8,6,5,3,0]}}